# What a knowledge graph should not index.
#
# Copy this to a project root as `.graphifyignore` BEFORE the first build:
#
#     cp ~/claudebase/templates/project-graphifyignore .graphifyignore
#
# Order matters. graphify's semantic pass reads prose with an LLM at roughly
# 5 min per chunk, serially on the claude-cli backend — an exclusion added after
# the build does not refund the extraction it already paid for. Every rule below
# was added mid-run on a live vault, which is the expensive way to learn them.
#
# Syntax is gitignore's, and graphify already honours .gitignore on top of this
# file, so node_modules/ and friends need no entry here.


# Everything hidden — dot-directories AND dotfiles, at any depth. None of it is
# corpus content: it is tooling config and harness state (.claude/, .omp/,
# .github/, .mcp.json) plus the graph's own artifacts under .graphify/. A single
# `.*` covers files and directories both, and covers dot-dirs added later.
#
# Verified against graphify's own detect() on a fixture tree: `.*` drops
# .claude/skills/SKILL.md, .mcp.json, and .obsidian/plugin.js while keeping
# 0_Project/note.md, README.md, and 0_Project/run.py.
#
# The measured case for the biggest one, kept because it is the evidence:
# .obsidian/ is vendored plugin and theme JS, and a --code-only build of one
# vault produced 16,954 nodes of which 16,044 (94%) came from there, leaving 806
# for everything actually written by hand. A graph that is 94% someone else's
# bundled JS answers no question you would ask it.
.*

# Build artifacts of the graph itself, for repos predating GRAPHIFY_OUT=.graphify.
graphify-out/

# Images and video. Semantic extraction sends these through a vision pass, and
# on one vault the chunk covering a project's photos/ and videos/ timed out
# after the full 600 s and produced nothing — ten minutes burned for zero nodes,
# with 681 such files tracked. A screenshot of a plot contributes almost nothing
# to a graph of concepts, which is what the corpus is for.
#
# PDFs are deliberately NOT here: those are papers, and their text is exactly
# the kind of content a concept graph should carry.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.webp
*.svg
*.heic
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm

# Matching is case-sensitive: the lowercase list above let 7 `.PNG` files
# through on the first attempt. Uppercase variants for the extensions a camera
# or a screenshot tool actually produces.
*.PNG
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.HEIC
*.MP4
*.MOV

